<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31968" root="غضر" body-key="g">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا نَامَ لِغُضْرٍ</span></b>  is expl. as meaning <i>He hardly,</i> or
<i>scarcely, slept;</i> but is said to be with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ع</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ص</span>, and
has been thus mentioned before [in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عصر</span>]. (TA.)

